                <pb facs="0706" n="626" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg626"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-10"><hi rendition="#italic">August 10,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Powell reports that Admiral Killick prevents the steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Paloma</hi> from entering Cape Haitian; that he has
                    cabled to Commander McCrea, at Gonaives, that the Haitian Government is not
                    recognized, nor the blockade of the Cape, and to give protection to any
                    American, Cuban, or foreign vessel desiring to enter Cape, informing Admiral
                    Killick of his intention.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
